# 1. Why Document Challenges

A successful implementation guide should not record only the final working configuration.

It should also preserve:

- What failed
- What the symptoms looked like
- What assumptions were wrong
- What diagnostics were used
- What the actual root cause was
- What fixed the issue
- How the architecture changed afterward

The objective is to make the HomeLab reproducible and easier to troubleshoot in the future.

---

# 2. Troubleshooting Philosophy

The HomeAuto troubleshooting approach follows one primary rule:

> **Validate the failure at the lowest possible layer before changing higher-level services.**

For example:

```text
Home Assistant automation missing?
           â”‚
           â–¼
Was HA sensor updated?
           â”‚
           â–¼
Did MQTT/API contain the data?
           â”‚
           â–¼
Did Frigate create the event?
           â”‚
           â–¼
Did detection work?
           â”‚
           â–¼
Was the camera stream valid?
```

This prevents multiple components from being changed simultaneously.

