<a id="challenge-compose-v1-v2"></a>

# 4. Challenge â€” Docker Compose v1 vs v2 Confusion
## Symptom

The environment initially attempted to use:

```bash
docker-compose
```

and also attempted to install:

```text
docker-compose-plugin
```

The system returned:

```text
Unable to locate package docker-compose-plugin
```

and the legacy command:

```bash
docker-compose
```

was unavailable.

## Root Cause

Docker Compose exists in different generations.

Older documentation often uses:

```text
docker-compose
```

while the current HomeLab uses:

```text
docker compose
```

as part of the Docker CLI.

## Working Environment

The HomeLab ultimately standardized on:

```text
Docker 29.1.3
```

and:

```text
Docker Compose v2.40.3+ds1
```

Verify:

```bash
docker --version
```

```bash
docker compose version
```

## Resolution

All HomeAuto documentation and scripts were standardized on:

```bash
docker compose
```

## Engineering Lesson

> **Confirm the installed toolchain before following version-specific tutorials.**

Commands from older tutorials should not be copied blindly into a modern environment.

