<a id="challenge-multiple-stacks"></a>

# 5. Challenge â€” Managing Multiple Compose Stacks
## Symptom

As more services were introduced, commands became increasingly repetitive.

For example:

```bash
docker compose \
  --env-file ~/docker/.env \
  -f ~/docker/stacks/frigate.yml \
  restart
```

Every stack required a different path.

This made routine operations harder to remember and increased the possibility of restarting the wrong application.

## Root Cause

The multi-stack architecture improved isolation but introduced operational complexity.

```text
Better Architecture
       â”‚
       â–¼
More Compose Files
       â”‚
       â–¼
More Commands
```

## Resolution

A custom lifecycle controller was created:

```text
~/docker/dockerctl
```

It provides commands such as:

```bash
./dockerctl start-all
```

```bash
./dockerctl stop-all
```

```bash
./dockerctl status
```

and:

```bash
./dockerctl restart frigate frigate
```

## Engineering Lesson

> **Architecture and operations must evolve together.**

Splitting services improves isolation, but the operator still needs a simple control interface.

