<a id="challenge-service-restart"></a>

# 6. Challenge â€” Restarting One Service Without Affecting Others
## Symptom

The first `dockerctl` implementation operated mainly at the stack level.

For example:

```bash
./dockerctl restart infrastructure
```

would restart everything inside:

```text
infrastructure.yml
```

including:

```text
Portainer
Dozzle
```

even when only one service required maintenance.

## Root Cause

The controller called:

```bash
docker compose restart
```

against the complete Compose file rather than an individual service.

## Resolution

The service controller was enhanced to support:

```bash
./dockerctl restart <stack> <service>
```

Examples:

```bash
./dockerctl restart infrastructure portainer
```

```bash
./dockerctl restart infrastructure dozzle
```

```bash
./dockerctl restart mqtt mqtt
```

```bash
./dockerctl restart frigate frigate
```

```bash
./dockerctl restart homeassistant homeassistant
```

## Result

Example:

```text
./dockerctl restart frigate frigate

Frigate          RESTARTED

MQTT             UNCHANGED
Home Assistant   UNCHANGED
Portainer        UNCHANGED
Dozzle           UNCHANGED
WebSSH           UNCHANGED
```

## Engineering Lesson

The resulting operational principle is:

> **Restart only what changed. Verify what restarted. Leave everything else running.**

