<a id="challenge-portainer-timeout"></a>

# 8. Challenge â€” Portainer Initial Administrator Timeout
## Symptom

Portainer repeatedly displayed the initial administrator setup page.

Logs indicated a state similar to:

```text
No administrator account configured
```

The setup process could also expire if not completed within the allowed initialization period.

## Root Cause

Portainer protects the first-user bootstrap process with a limited setup window.

If the administrator account is not created in time, the initialization session may expire.

## Resolution

Restart Portainer only:

```bash
cd ~/docker
./dockerctl restart infrastructure portainer
```

Verify:

```bash
./dockerctl status infrastructure portainer
```

Then reopen:

```text
https://<UBUNTU_VM_IP>:9443
```

and complete the administrator setup promptly.

## Engineering Lesson

> **Application-level setup timeouts do not necessarily indicate container failure.**

The container state and application state must be distinguished.

