# 31. Architecture Decisions Resulting from Challenges

Several important architecture decisions came directly from troubleshooting.

| Challenge | Architecture Decision |
|---|---|
| Empty Compose file | Move to explicit stack files |
| Many Compose files | Create `dockerctl` |
| Stack-wide restart | Add service-level lifecycle |
| Dependency ordering | Add `start-all` / `stop-all` sequencing |
| MQTT permissions | Standardize persistent-storage permissions |
| Portainer timeout | Support isolated service restart |
| Camera troubleshooting | Validate stream before AI |
| Missing HA event | Validate Frigate API first |
| LPR MQTT inconsistency | Add REST/API integration path |
| Face recognition incomplete | Use explicit validation states |
| HA YAML changes | Restart HA only |
| AI complexity | Validate CPU functionality before acceleration |
| Light-mode failure | Adopt semantic CSS variables |
| Ambiguous metrics | Scope metrics to specific systems |

