# 42. Engineering Principles Derived from the HomeLab

The challenges encountered during implementation produced several recurring principles.

### Validate the source first

```text
Source data before integration debugging.
```

### Restart only what changed

```text
Avoid unnecessary service disruption.
```

### Keep failure domains separate

```text
Camera â‰  Frigate â‰  MQTT â‰  Home Assistant.
```

### Prefer reproducible commands

```text
Operational procedures should be scriptable.
```

### Persist configuration outside containers

```text
Containers are disposable.
Configuration is not.
```

### Optimize only after functionality is proven

```text
Correctness first.
Performance second.
```

### Keep Lab and Production distinct

```text
Validated in Lab does not automatically mean Production ready.
```

